        "node_id": "n_1_6f852f",
        "thought_text": "Consider the parity of N. If N is even, Alice can always ensure she gets at least as many high-value cards as Bob by taking the highest available card on her turn.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794501222.9572432
      },
      "rev_n_2_b0d205_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_b0d205_0",
        "node_id": "n_2_b0d205",
        "thought_text": "If N is odd, Alice can still aim to get more points by strategically choosing cards that maximize her advantage over Bob, considering the sequence of turns.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794501222.9572568
      },
      "rev_n_3_b5892d_0": {
